WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.582
- I'm here with none other
than Natalie Portman!

00:00:02.582 --> 00:00:04.173
(audience clapping)

00:00:04.173 --> 00:00:05.780
Oh my God!

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:08.700
Natalie recently wrote a
fantastic children's book

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.750
called Natalie Portman's Fables,

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.680
which is why I thought I'd challenge her

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.606
to a game called,

00:00:13.606 --> 00:00:16.424
are you able to label this fable?

00:00:16.424 --> 00:00:17.864
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.864 --> 00:00:22.344
♪ Are you able to label this fable ♪

00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:23.330
(laughing)

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.260
Oh my God,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.710
here's how it works.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.550
We'll each get a clue that leads us

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.200
like a trail of breadcrumbs

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.600
to the title of a famous fable.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.760
If Natalie or I can name
that fable, we get a point.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.410
If we don't know or give the wrong answer,

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.710
the other person can steal for two points.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.390
Uh oh, plot twist.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.990
Most points wins.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.030
If Natalie wins,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.540
her photo will be added to

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.660
the Blake Shelton wall of champions

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.230
who beat Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.152
Not many people on it,
Natalie, no pressure.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:53.480
(laughing)
Immediately following the show

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.600
that will happen,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.060
but that's not all, if Natalie wins,

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.780
the left side of the
audience is going home

00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.210
with a special prize.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.220
If I win the right side is getting it,

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.500
but wait, we need a host

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.480
'cause I can't do both, exactly.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.850
Here to lend a hand is a very funny woman

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.720
whom you can see each Wednesday
in The Goldbergs on ABC,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.480
let's give it up for Wendi McLendon-Covey!

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.909
(upbeat music)

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.909
(audience cheering)

00:01:28.077 --> 00:01:30.410
Oh, you win for best outfit.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:34.870
- Well, thank you, you
win for sexiest audience.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:35.944
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes!
- And hello, Natalie.

00:01:35.944 --> 00:01:37.290
(laughing)

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.000
All right, are we jumping right in?

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.830
- Let's, okay wait, so here we go.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.349
So you already said hello to Wendi.

00:01:42.349 --> 00:01:43.820
- [Wendi McLendon-Covey] Yes.
- So thank you for being here,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.002
first of all and in the
most fabulous suit ever

00:01:46.002 --> 00:01:48.700
and for hosting our game.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.560
Take it away you can go.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.620
- Okay, first question is for Natalie.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.453
- [Kelly Clarkson] Uh oh.

00:01:52.453 --> 00:01:54.310
- If the slipper fits

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.773
this handsome fella will
ask for the hand of blank.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:00.896
- Cinderella.

00:02:00.896 --> 00:02:01.729
- [Wendi McLendon-Covey] All right.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:02.860
(dinging)

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.345
One point for Natalie.

00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:05.690
- Boo, okay.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:06.960
(laughing)

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.800
- [Wendi McLendon-Covey] Okay,
next question is for Kelly.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.700
She skipped merrily off,
not abiding the wood,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.200
that's when the Wolf saw--

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.565
- Little Red Riding Hood.

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:17.398
- [Wendi McLendon-Covey] Yes,
(dinging)

00:02:17.398 --> 00:02:18.231
correct.
- Yes!

00:02:18.231 --> 00:02:20.195
- Point for Kelly.
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes.

00:02:20.195 --> 00:02:21.270
- Again--
- No pressure Natalie,

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:22.860
you're doing fine, don't worry about it.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.320
- Back to Natalie.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.130
So different she floated as,

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.400
so different she floated
along as a suckling,

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.393
she'd grow to be gorgeous this blank.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.410
- The Ugly Little Duckling?

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:39.243
- [Wendi McLendon-Covey] Yes.
(dinging)

00:02:39.243 --> 00:02:40.490
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes,
The Ugly Duckling, yes.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:41.323
- The Ugly Ducking?

00:02:41.323 --> 00:02:42.520
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes, yes.
(audience cheering)

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.080
- Okay, next one for Kelly.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.427
- Nicely done, whatever Natalie.

00:02:45.427 --> 00:02:48.570
(laughing)
- Thanks.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.403
Good luck.

00:02:49.403 --> 00:02:51.060
(laughing)

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.480
- All right, Kelly you're up.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.510
The mattresses rose as high as a tree,

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.370
but sleep would not come for the,

00:02:58.370 --> 00:02:59.749
